      "content": "Interesting. You mentioned the suburban context might \"appeal to credit algorithms focused on economic stability.\" Can you expand on that? Why would an algorithm treat an urban residence like Westside Heights as a higher risk factor if the income and credit score are exactly the same? Is there some kind of correlation between those types of neighborhoods and default rates that we should be accounting for?",
